<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman cuts Rank to &quot;neutral&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman cuts Rank to &quot;neutral&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rank Group Plc was cut to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; at Lehman Brothers, the investment bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In a research note, Lehamn analyst Fraser Ramzan said the move followed a review after a poor trading performance in the past five months.</p>
<p>He said Rank had potential and value in the use of its balance sheet but this was likely to take time to impact on profit growth.</p>
<p>The stock was up 1/2p at 361 by 0824 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
